From: Austin Lane <vidplace7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Remove the mesh-analysis console script

The mesh-analysis tool is an analysis UI built on
dash, plotly and pyarrow. None of those are packaged for
OpenWrt or defined in the package dependencies.
The generated /usr/bin/mesh-analysis entrypoint can never run.
Drop it so the package does not ship a broken executable.

--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -73,7 +73,6 @@ analysis = ["dash", "dash-bootstrap-comp
 [tool.poetry.scripts]
 meshtastic = "meshtastic.__main__:main"
 mesh-tunnel = "meshtastic.__main__:tunnelMain [tunnel]"
-mesh-analysis = "meshtastic.analysis.__main__:main [analysis]"
 
 # "Poe the poet" (optional) provides an easy way of running non python tools inside the poetry virtualenv
 # if you would like to use it run "pipx install poe"
